# The depot's flow, written by yardr depot init. yardr reads it from the base
# branch; see docs/flows.md.
#
# The three ways back to new (changes from review, changes from review-security,
# failed from the assembly) are limited to 3 rounds together, as the starter pack
# has them: the fourth goes to decide, where a person reads its note. The train
# flow (yardr.train.flow) has no limit.
backlog -> shape | new | decide
shape -> new on done | decide on question | backlog
new -> review on done | decide on question | backlog
review -> review-security on done | approved on done-safe | new on changes max 3 then decide | decide on question
review-security -> approved on done | new on changes max 3 then decide | decide on question
approved -> merged on done | new on failed max 3 then decide | decide on question
decide -> backlog | new
merged terminal
